{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794404722,"nonce":"Bnjn4ppjf+Irz78cUQuk4swfhIU=","title":"Error-controlled marches pay for every unused attempt of the max_steps budget","message":"The adaptive march is a fixed-length lax.scan over max_steps attempts; once t1 is reached the settled tail still runs one (no-op) scan iteration per remaining attempt. On a 2-D P1 heat march at rtol 1e-6, bdf() with the default max_steps=1000 runs measurably slower than the same march with max_steps=120 (identical result), so a large share of the run is the idle tail. Same root as the memory growth with max_steps. Fix direction: a chunked scan that skips whole settled chunks, or a checkpointed bounded while loop (reverse-differentiable).","files":null}]}